// title: NTLM logons by device and account, last 7 days, to scope where IAKerb removes the fallback
// date: 2026-11-19
// product: Defender for Endpoint
// tables: DeviceLogonEvents
// purpose: Counts logons whose Protocol is NTLM per device, account and logon type, with the remote IPs seen, so the NTLM-retirement plan starts from measured use rather than from a guess. Not run against a tenant in this pass.
// source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/defender-xdr/advanced-hunting-devicelogonevents-table
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
// Microsoft SOC Brief 19 Nov 2026 - where NTLM is still used, before IAKerb
// Columns as on the DeviceLogonEvents reference cited beside this query. Not run against a tenant in this pass.
DeviceLogonEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| where Protocol =~ "NTLM"
| summarize Logons = count(), Failed = countif(ActionType == "LogonFailed"), RemoteIPs = make_set(RemoteIP, 20)
          by DeviceName, AccountDomain, AccountName, LogonType
| sort by Logons desc
